# Example EnvironmentFile for cathedral-publisher.service (thin publisher —
# serves the SIGNED weight vector the consolidated validator fetches locally).
# Install as /etc/cathedral-publisher/cathedral-publisher.env, mode 0600,
# owned by cathedral-publisher. COMMIT NO SECRETS.

# --- signing (REQUIRED) -----------------------------------------------------
CATHEDRAL_EVAL_SIGNING_KEY=<ed25519-signing-key>

# --- weight policy identity -------------------------------------------------
CATHEDRAL_WEIGHT_POLICY_KEY_ID=cathedral-weight-policy
CATHEDRAL_WEIGHT_POLICY_NETUID=39

# --- storage ----------------------------------------------------------------
CATHEDRAL_DB_PATH=/var/lib/cathedral-publisher/publisher.db
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://<user>:<pass>@<host>:5432/<db>

# --- allocation contract (v2 default) ---------------------------------------
# The consolidated validator's config/validator-selfcompose-sn39.toml pins the
# validator to require_policy = "validated_supply_v1" (v2). Keep this side on v2
# too until the paired Phase 5 flip. See deploy/publisher/README.md.
# CATHEDRAL_ALLOCATION_CONTRACT=v3
# CATHEDRAL_WEIGHT_POLICY_FORCED_BURN_PERCENTAGE_V2=10

# --- serving ----------------------------------------------------------------
# This role binds the local address the validator's [publisher] url points at
# (127.0.0.1:8010 by default; see the unit + validator-selfcompose-sn39.toml).
WEB_CONCURRENCY=2
